# 🐳 Containers

## ▶️ Run

```bash
docker run -d --name app01 image:v1
```

With port:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -p 9090:8080 \
  image:v1
```

With environment:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -e APP_ENV=production \
  image:v1
```

With resource limits:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  --memory=512m \
  --cpus="1.0" \
  image:v1
```

With restart policy:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  image:v1
```

---

## 🎛️ Manage

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Running containers | `docker ps` |
| All containers | `docker ps -a` |
| Start | `docker start app01` |
| Stop | `docker stop app01` |
| Restart | `docker restart app01` |
| Remove | `docker rm app01` |
| Force remove | `docker rm -f app01` |
| Processes | `docker top app01` |

