# 🔌 Ports

### Remember

```text
-p HOST:CONTAINER
```

Example:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -p 9090:8080 \
  image:v1
```

```text
Browser
   │
   ▼
HOST :9090
   │
   ▼
CONTAINER :8080
   │
   ▼
Application
```

Check:

```bash
docker ps
docker port app01
```

Test:

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:9090
```

### EXPOSE vs `-p`

| Dockerfile | Runtime |
|---|---|
| `EXPOSE 8080` | `-p 9090:8080` |
| Documents port | Publishes port |

> [!NOTE]
> `EXPOSE` does **not** publish the port.

