# 🐳 Dockerfile

### Production-style structure

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.12-slim

WORKDIR /app

RUN useradd -m -s /bin/bash appuser

COPY app.py .

ARG APP_VERSION=1.0

ENV APP_ENV=production

RUN chown -R appuser:appuser /app

USER appuser

EXPOSE 8080

HEALTHCHECK --interval=10s --timeout=3s --retries=3 \
  CMD python -c "import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen('http://localhost:8080/health')"

CMD ["python", "app.py"]
```

---

## 🧩 Instructions

| Instruction | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `FROM` | Base image |
| `WORKDIR` | Working directory |
| `COPY` | Copy files |
| `RUN` | Build-time command |
| `ARG` | Build-time variable |
| `ENV` | Runtime/default variable |
| `USER` | Runtime user |
| `EXPOSE` | Port metadata |
| `HEALTHCHECK` | Application health |
| `CMD` | Default runtime command |
| `ENTRYPOINT` | Main executable |

---

## 🧠 Build vs Runtime

| 🏗️ BUILD TIME | ▶️ RUN TIME |
|---|---|
| `ARG` | `ENV` |
| `RUN` | `CMD` |

```text
ARG → docker build
ENV → docker run

RUN → builds image
CMD → starts application
```

---

## 👤 Non-root User

```dockerfile
RUN useradd -m -s /bin/bash appuser

COPY . /app

RUN chown -R appuser:appuser /app

USER appuser
```

Order:

```text
Create User
    ↓
Copy Files
    ↓
Set Ownership
    ↓
Switch User
    ↓
Run Application
```

